# Question folder contract

Every `questions/<slug>/` folder must include:

- `README.md` — problem, sources, requirements, APIs, high-level design, data model, deep dives, how to run locally, interview checklist
- `FAQ.md` — interview Q&A (requirements, design choices, tradeoffs, what the local system taught)
- `FLOW.md` — mermaid flowchart and/or sequence diagrams for happy path, writes, reads, failure
- `COMPONENTS.md` — each important piece: definition + role in *this* design
- `docker-compose.yml` — local mocked components
- `scripts/setup.sh` — bring the stack up
- `scripts/run-scenarios.sh` — integration-style scenarios against running containers
- `src/` — application code
- `tests/` — scenario helpers or extra tests

Status in README: **Stub** (placeholders), **Designed** (docs filled, no running system), or **Implemented** (setup + scenarios work).

Slug is kebab-case. Overlapping names from Hello Interview and Alex Xu share one folder.
